description:
FILED s543k (Opus 5.5, 2026-11-22), found by member 2's probe b05 (#5270): the span route (a file lexical used in a later package section) and the capture route (a file lexical a named sub captures) answer the same.  PRE-EXISTING: base 4a0fd0ec.

REPRODUCER (perl 5.40.3 | ./runpcl):
    sub early { defined(eval q{$x}) ? "d" : "u" }
    my $x = "lex";
    sub g { $x }
    print early(), " ", g(), "\n";
        perl  u lex        PCL  d lex

WHAT IT IS: the lexical is promoted under its OWN name (the identity cell: one declaration file-wide, the file never spells `$main::x`), so the cell IS the package variable `$main::x`; the eval in `early` gets no pair (the binder says its pad does not see the declaration -- right) and falls through to the package global, which is the lexical's cell.  s543k's #5270 fixed the MANGLED span cell (no M-F alias in the program unit); the identity cell has no alias to drop -- the shared symbol is the identity.  FIX DIRECTION (not designed): in a file with a string eval whose word does NOT see the declaration and that names the canon (Parser2::_eval_operand_may_name), take the mangle instead of identity (`_own_name_cell_ok` false); measure what moves (every identity cell in an eval file would become a mangle).
